From: OmacVM
Subject: [PATCH] cocoa: FullPanel's state lets go of a window that is freed

What: a window's FullPanel state now hangs on the window through a small
owner object that only the window holds. When the window is freed, the
owner tells the state first (windowGone): it forgets the window, stops
observing, and puts the menu bar and the app's presentation back without
asking the window anything (releaseSystemState). Blocks and observers that
still hold the state (a return check after a Space change, the
presentation observer) find no window and do nothing.

Why: #402. A VM started in "Full screen including notch" (OMACVM_FULLPANEL=1)
died when the display its window was on was unplugged: macOS took the
windows out of full screen, the display's own window (one window per display)
was closed, and when AppKit's exit-full-screen transition let go of it the
window was freed. Freeing it freed its state, whose dealloc asked the half
freed window -isKeyWindow (SIGSEGV in -[NSWindow isKeyWindow] under
-[OmacVMFullPanelState dealloc], crash report on the Mac mini 2026-10-14).
The state kept an unretained pointer to its window. (The same owner, kept
for the reservation-based FullPanel of omacvm-cocoa-fullpanel.patch.)

Upstream: not sent (OmacVM's FullPanel).
Test: app/runtime/Tests/display/test-fullpanel-window-gone.sh (the wiring in
the patched ui/cocoa.m at build time); src/tests/e2e/display-unplug.sh (a
virtual display unplugged under a real VM, also with FullPanel; the release
gate). Applies after omacvm-cocoa-fullpanel-scale.patch.

--- a/ui/cocoa.m
+++ b/ui/cocoa.m
@@ -3337,15 +3337,30 @@ - (id)initWithWindow:(NSWindow *)w;
 - (bool)claimsStrip;
 - (void)willEnterFullScreen;
 - (void)releaseSystemState;
+- (void)windowGone;
 @end
 
 static char omacvm_fullpanel_state_key;
 static char omacvm_fullpanel_titlebar_context;
 static char omacvm_fullpanel_options_context;
 
+/*
+ * A window's state hangs on it through this owner, which only the window
+ * holds: freed with the window, it tells the state the window is gone
+ * before anything else can use it (#402).
+ */
+@interface OmacVMFullPanelOwner : NSObject
+{
+@public
+    OmacVMFullPanelState *state;
+}
+@end
+
 static OmacVMFullPanelState *omacvm_fullpanel_state(NSWindow *window)
 {
-    return window ? objc_getAssociatedObject(window, &omacvm_fullpanel_state_key) : nil;
+    OmacVMFullPanelOwner *owner = window ?
+        objc_getAssociatedObject(window, &omacvm_fullpanel_state_key) : nil;
+    return owner ? owner->state : nil;
 }
 
 /* The guest's size, the full-screen area and the display box use the whole display. */
@@ -3544,6 +3559,22 @@ - (id)initWithWindow:(NSWindow *)w
     return self;
 }
 
+/*
+ * The window is being freed (OmacVMFullPanelOwner), e.g. a display's window
+ * closed while macOS took it out of full screen because its display was
+ * unplugged (#402): it must not be asked anything any more. Blocks and
+ * observers that still hold this state find no window; the menu bar and the
+ * app's presentation come back without it (the rules need it only while
+ * the strip is covered).
+ */
+- (void)windowGone
+{
+    window = nil;
+    [[[NSWorkspace sharedWorkspace] notificationCenter] removeObserver:self];
+    [[NSNotificationCenter defaultCenter] removeObserver:self];
+    [self releaseSystemState];
+}
+
 - (void)dealloc
 {
     [self releaseSystemState];
@@ -4260,18 +4291,28 @@ - (void)observeValueForKeyPath:(NSString *)keyPath
 
 @end
 
+@implementation OmacVMFullPanelOwner
+- (void)dealloc
+{
+    [state windowGone];
+    [state release];
+    [super dealloc];
+}
+@end
+
 /* A VM window's FullPanel state, made before its first full screen. */
 static void omacvm_fullpanel_prepare_window(NSWindow *window)
 {
-    OmacVMFullPanelState *state;
+    OmacVMFullPanelOwner *owner;
 
     if (!window || omacvm_fullpanel_state(window)) {
         return;
     }
-    state = [[OmacVMFullPanelState alloc] initWithWindow:window];
-    objc_setAssociatedObject(window, &omacvm_fullpanel_state_key, state,
+    owner = [[OmacVMFullPanelOwner alloc] init];
+    owner->state = [[OmacVMFullPanelState alloc] initWithWindow:window];
+    objc_setAssociatedObject(window, &omacvm_fullpanel_state_key, owner,
                              OBJC_ASSOCIATION_RETAIN_NONATOMIC);
-    [state release];
+    [owner release];
 }
 
 /* The VM's windows: the main one and the other displays' (external displays on). */
